# Milestone workflow

This project should be developed milestone by milestone.

For each milestone:

1. Plan the milestone before coding.
2. Write or update tests first.
3. Confirm the new tests fail for the expected reason where practical.
4. Implement the smallest amount of code needed to pass the tests.
5. Run the full Godot test command.
6. Fix errors until all tests pass.
7. Summarise the tests that prove the milestone is complete.
8. Stop and wait for human review before moving to the next milestone.

Do not weaken or delete tests to make them pass.

Do not implement future milestones early.

The test command is:

& "C:\Tools\Godot\godot.exe" --headless --path "C:\Users\joesa\Documents\Cursor\BoardGame\gods-and-wizards\godot_game" -s res://tests/test_runner.gd

